# A stylesheet link's load and error events (HTML §4.6.7): one in the
# markup, three inserted by script — a sheet the page already has, a new
# one, one that is not there — each heard of in a task of its own (`during`
# is how many were heard while the script that inserted them ran: none), and
# a link whose href changes, heard of once for each sheet it names.
# link-events.html writes what it heard into its title half a second in,
# sorted. The clock moves in steps, as a window's turns do.
resize 800 600
open link-events.html
advance 100 7
assert-title during 0 | again:load | fresh:load | missing:error | moved:load | moved:load | parsed:load
